{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01YN3JAJvUwZCyZG6KNiJt7U", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.\n id |      name      \n----+----------------\n 58 | Kestrel Dental\n(1 row)\n\n id  | customer_id | amount_cents | status |       issued_at        \n-----+-------------+--------------+--------+------------------------\n 163 |          58 |         4900 | paid   | 2026-03-09 01:32:00+00\n 164 |          58 |         4900 | open   | 2026-04-06 01:32:00+00\n 165 |          58 |         4900 | open   | 2026-10-01 09:00:00+00\n 166 |          58 |         4900 | open   | 2026-10-01 09:01:00+00\n(4 rows)", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c1d34c3e-8996-4729-ab07-8da990171121", "uuid": "9334e312-2654-4da3-a521-78a896b8d930", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T13:16:41.802Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.\n id |      name      \n----+----------------\n 58 | Kestrel Dental\n(1 row)\n\n id  | customer_id | amount_cents | status |       issued_at        \n-----+-------------+--------------+--------+------------------------\n 163 |          58 |         4900 | paid   | 2026-03-09 01:32:00+00\n 164 |          58 |         4900 | open   | 2026-04-06 01:32:00+00\n 165 |          58 |         4900 | open   | 2026-10-01 09:00:00+00\n 166 |          58 |         4900 | open   | 2026-10-01 09:01:00+00\n(4 rows)", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01YN3JAJvUwZCyZG6KNiJt7U", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "subcommandResults"}}]}
